            <ArticleTitle>[Meningiosis--an additional cause of paraparesis in old dogs].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>480-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Based on a case report, occasionally observed, degenerative changes of the spinal meninx in a sense of meningiosis are presented that are not yet described. The patient was a thirteen-year-old dog, showing paraparesis and spinal pain. Findings of X-Ray examination, surgery and histology are described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
